PHP: disable session upload progress in generated configurations

https://www.php.net/archive/2026.php#2026-10-23-1

Mitigate CVE-2026-115560, the session serializer follow-up to
CVE-2026-109619, as recommended by PHP on 2026-10-23. Apply this before
request parsing through the generated php.ini, including buildEnv and
withExtensions used by devenv. Explicit extraConfig can override it.

Only configuration and wrappers change: the patched PHP interpreters and
extensions retain their upstream store paths. Raw unwrapped PHP and
applications replacing PHP_INI_SCAN_DIR need their own mitigation.
Remove this default when upstream releases the remaining source fix.

--- a/pkgs/development/interpreters/php/generic.nix
+++ b/pkgs/development/interpreters/php/generic.nix
@@ -142,6 +142,7 @@
             extNames = map getExtName enabledExtensions;
             extraInit = writeText "php-extra-init-${version}.ini" ''
               ${lib.concatStringsSep "\n" (lib.textClosureList extensionTexts extNames)}
+              session.upload_progress.enabled=0
               ${extraConfig}
             '';
 
